  "limitations": [
    "Server 2008 SP1 x86 build 6001 yields three matching full 17-field records. Native remains partial with 561 TrapFrame/list/symbol diagnostics. This proves equality of recovered rows on this sample, not exhaustive thread coverage.",
    "All Symbol0-Symbol3 fields are absent in both real outputs. Nonempty exact export symbol attribution is exercised by synthetic fixtures only; real successful external PDB attribution remains unverified.",
    "Win10/Win11/Win7/Server2003 output is empty in both engines and remains negative evidence. Every native output retains incomplete coverage diagnostics; empty output does not prove absence.",
    "TrapFrame must be a canonical kernel pointer and owner processes pass native EPROCESS checks. Native corruption and missing-page diagnostics intentionally expose skipped views; smeared-memory behavior may differ from the reference.",
    "Dr7 is returned as a decimal integer, Dr0-Dr3 are absolute hex addresses; only Dr7==0, State==4, four zero addresses, absent owner file VADs or all addresses outside file VADs suppress a readable row.",
    "File VAD lookup is half-open. Module names are normalized only for symbol lookup and exact address queries are batched across threads. No nearest-symbol guesses are made. First-module differences in PESymbols prototype-page recovery also apply.",
    "Pointer-width reads, legacy ownership precedence, absent TrapFrame/Dr fields, cancellation, row retention at resource limits and exact export resolution have synthetic coverage. Broader corrupt layouts and all failure contracts still need differential acceptance.",
    "ARM64 is explicitly unsupported. Result caching remains disabled because external PDB resources are not tracked as cache dependencies.",
    "Original user Debian image is unavailable; its page-table failure has not been accepted on the original sample."
  ]
